# A Luxel library scene (Gitea #785) — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# `fit tile`: one 7x7 sprite repeated across the layout and ADDED over a
# pattern. Two things worth knowing are in these four lines. The box is an
# EXPLICIT 64x64, not 0x0: a sprite layer with a zero box draws once at its
# natural size and `fit` means nothing (docs/spec/scenes.md §4), so `tile`
# needs somewhere to tile into. And the pattern runs at 60 % so the sparks have
# somewhere to add INTO — added over a saturated frame they are invisible.
S - Spark Field
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 60 none fill 1
N Twirls
I @pat/2d-spiral-twirls
L sprite 0 0 64 64 add 100 none tile 1
N Sparks
I @spr/spark
